# The page object of the "/legacy/" tree.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL
#
# The "/" tree is themed by EXT:bootstrap_package, which delivers everything it
# has through site sets and nothing through a static template: version 15 still
# shipped "Configuration/TypoScript/" and registered it with addStaticFile(),
# version 16 removed both ("[!!!][TASK] Migrate TypoScript configuration to site
# sets"). The "core-13" instance runs 15 and the "core-14" instance runs 16, so a
# "sys_template" record naming the theme renders one instance and renders nothing
# at all in the other.
#
# The "/legacy/" tree therefore cannot be themed. It is delivered the way an
# installation that predates site sets is delivered, and there is no pre-site-set
# delivery of that theme any more. What it gets instead is this: the smallest
# page object that puts the content of a page on the page, so the tree renders
# and the content elements and plugins of the academic extensions can be compared
# with the ones the site set driven tree renders.
#
# It is shipped twice, in the two forms a development instance needs it in - as
# this static template folder, named by the "include_static_file" of the legacy
# root "sys_template" record, and as the site set "fgtclb/academics-dev-site-page-object",
# whose "setup.typoscript" imports this file. The set is what
# "LegacyDeliveryTest" puts in the place of the theme on the "/" side, so that
# both trees are rendered by the same text and a difference the test reports is a
# difference in what the academic extensions deliver.

page = PAGE
page {
    typeNum = 0

    10 = COA
    10 {
        10 = TEXT
        10.data = page:title
        10.wrap = <h1>|</h1>

        20 < styles.content.get
    }

    meta.viewport = width=device-width, initial-scale=1
}

config {
    # Absolute paths, so a link of the mirrored tree differs from its original by
    # the "/legacy" segment and by nothing else.
    absRefPrefix = /
    # An exception in a content element is something to see, not something to
    # replace with a box that renders the same on both sides of a comparison.
    contentObjectExceptionHandler = 0
    disablePrefixComment = 1
    headerComment = Delivered by the static template of EXT:academics_dev_site.
}
